{"id":"mayor_louisville-ky_craig-greenberg","n":"Craig Greenberg","p":"Democratic","race":{"mode":"mayor","st":"KY","d":null,"city":"louisville-ky"},"updated":"2026-11-09","bio":"Craig Greenberg (born August 22, 1973) is an American businessman, lawyer, and politician serving since 2023 as the third mayor of the consolidated city-county of Louisville, Kentucky. During his mayoral campaign, he was the target of an assassination attempt at his campaign headquarters, but emerged unscathed.","bioSrc":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craig_Greenberg","wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Craig_Greenberg","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Craig_Greenberg_announces_return_of_Thunder_Over_Louisville_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Craig_Greenberg_announces_return_of_Thunder_Over_Louisville_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","imgSrc":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Craig_Greenberg_announces_return_of_Thunder_Over_Louisville_(cropped).jpg","offices":["Mayor of Louisville, Kentucky (2023–present)"],"qid":"Q115180671"}